**What does this PR address? (Why)**
In LocalLivenessAnalyser, when computing outgoing and incoming live locals (OUT and IN), sets were merged using merge(set1, set2) which returned set2 reference directly whenever set1.isEmpty().
```java
  private Set<Local> merge(@NonNull Set<Local> set1, @NonNull Set<Local> set2) {
    if (set1.isEmpty()) {
      return set2;
    } else {
      set1.addAll(set2);
      return set1;
    }
  }
```
Later, when calculating outMinusDef for a statement, out.remove(def) was called directly on out. If out was aliased to a successor liveIn set, this removed the defined local directly from the successor live-in set in-place.


**What are the main implementation details? (What, How)**
1. Created fresh HashSet instances for out and never return aliased collection references from set union.
2. Cloned out into an independent outMinusDef set before mutating it with remove(def).
3. Removed not used anymore merge() method.
4. No need anymore to copy out, when adding it to liveOut map, as it is not mutated anymore(outMinusDef is created).
5. added extra null checks for successor edges received from liveIn.get(succ), null can occur with a malformed synthetic graph constructed manually


