**What does this PR address? (Why)**
In bytecode, the INSTANCEOF opcode takes an internal type name or array descriptor (JVMS §6.5). When checking against array types (such as byte[], Object[], or int[][]), the descriptor string provided to ASM TypeInsnNode is "[B", "[Ljava/lang/Object;", or "[[I".

Calling toJimpleClassType("[B") creates a JavaClassType whose class name is literally "[B", instead of an ArrayType with base type PrimitiveType.ByteType and dimension 1.

**What are the main implementation details? (What, How)**
use `arrayTypetoJimpleType` insteadof `AsmUtil.toJimpleClassType` for INSTANCE OF 

