Callbacks in `enqueueWrite()` were being added to `writeCallbacks` before validation, then invoked on error without removal, causing duplicate invocations when the queue was later cleared.

## Changes

- **`enqueueWrite()`**: Remove callback from `writeCallbacks` before invoking on disconnect error
- **`write()`**: Remove callback from `writeCallbacks` before invoking when `enqueueWrite()` fails for `WRITE_TYPE_DEFAULT` operations

```java
// Before: callback invoked but left in queue
if (!isConnected() || gatt == null) {
    if (withResponse && callback != null) {
        callback.invoke("Device is not connected", null);  // Still in writeCallbacks
    }
}

// After: callback removed before invocation
if (!isConnected() || gatt == null) {
    if (withResponse && callback != null) {
        writeCallbacks.removeLastOccurrence(callback);
        callback.invoke("Device is not connected", null);
    }
}
```

Ensures callbacks are invoked exactly once across all error paths.

